+For machine-readable output, run `python3 install.py list --json`. Standard output is
+one JSON object with `schema_version: 1` and a `skills` list sorted by name. Each entry
+contains `name`, `description`, sorted direct `dependencies` (skill names, without
+expanding transitive dependencies), and `roles`, which maps every supported host to
+sorted runtime role names. Hosts that install only skills have empty role lists.
+Both list formats validate the package and leave user configuration and installation
+directories untouched.
